				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-11550464#post-4244316</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-11550464/zetetic-bulletin:the-myth-of-the-wu-xing-iris#post-4244316</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 10 May 2019 10:38:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Etinjat</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4055881</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Nice&nbsp;work,but&nbsp;I&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;questions.</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;btw,who&nbsp;put&nbsp;the&nbsp;scp-_-j&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;goi&nbsp;con</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>1.Does the word mean &quot;五行&quot; in Chinese？</p> <blockquote> <p>Wu Xing</p> </blockquote> <p>If so,this word should be translated as &quot;the Five elements&quot; instead of &quot;Moving Star&quot;.</p> <p>2.</p> <blockquote> <p>traditional Chinese language.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p>middle-pinyin characters.</p> </blockquote> You mean&#8230;<em>Middle Chinese</em>?In fact,pinyin didn't appear until the 20st century.Before that, people used &quot;反切法&quot; to mark the pronunciation of Chinese characters.At the time, the word was pronounced &quot;<em>ŋuo ɦɑŋ</em>&quot;(presumed by 鄭張尚芳),not &quot;<em>Wu Xing</em>&quot; (in Mandarin).Well, seal script is usually used as decorative patterns in traditional Chinese crafts,like that:<br /> <img src="http://www.vividict.com/UserFiles/Image/==CE--shangye==/--CE4--shu(zu)--/006wu/41zh00.gif" alt="41zh00.gif" class="image" /> <img src="http://www.vividict.com/UserFiles/Image/==CD--jiaotong==/--CD2--xing(zu)--/001xing/[4]zhuan(1).gif" alt="[4]zhuan(1).gif" class="image" /></div> </div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
